    author: "Waptrix Team",
    image: "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551650975-87deedd944c3?w=1200&q=80",
    imageAlt: "WhatsApp Business API setup tutorial on laptop",
    metaDescription: "Step-by-step guide to setting up WhatsApp Business API in India 2026. Connect your number, get Meta approval, and send your first campaign in 30 minutes with Waptrix.",
    content: "## What You Need Before You Start\n\nSetting up the WhatsApp Business API used to require a Meta Partner and weeks of waiting. With Waptrix, you can do it yourself in under 30 minutes. Here's what you need:\n\n- **A Facebook Business Manager account** (free at business.facebook.com)\n- **A phone number** that is NOT already registered on WhatsApp (personal or business)\n- **Business details:** name, address, website, category\n- **An Indian business** (or a business operating in India)\n\nThe phone number you use must not be registered on WhatsApp already. If it is, you'll need to delete that WhatsApp account first.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Create a Facebook Business Manager Account\n\nGo to [business.facebook.com](https://business.facebook.com) and sign up. Enter your:\n- Business name (as it appears on legal documents)\n- Your name\n- Business email address\n\nVerify your email and complete business verification. This involves uploading a business document (GST certificate, shop registration, or utility bill in your business name).\n\n---\n\n## Step 2: Create a WhatsApp Business Account (WABA)\n\nInside Facebook Business Manager:\n1. Go to **Business Settings → Accounts → WhatsApp Accounts**\n2. Click **Add** → **Create a WhatsApp Business Account**\n3. Name your WABA (this appears to customers as your display name)\n4. Accept the WhatsApp Business terms of service\n\n---\n\n## Step 3: Add Your Phone Number\n\n1. Inside your WABA, go to **Phone Numbers → Add Phone Number**\n2. Enter the number you want to use for WhatsApp Business\n3. Choose verification method: **SMS** or **Voice call**\n4. Enter the 6-digit verification code\n\nYour number is now verified and connected to the WhatsApp Business API.\n\n---\n\n## Step 4: Connect to Waptrix\n\n1. Sign up at [app.waptrix.in](https://app.waptrix.in)\n2. Go to **Settings → Connect WhatsApp**\n3. Click **Connect via Meta** — this opens Meta's OAuth flow\n4. Select your Facebook Business Manager account\n5. Select the WABA you created in Step 2\n6. Select your phone number\n7. Click **Authorize**\n\nWaptrix automatically subscribes your WABA to the necessary webhooks and imports your phone number settings.\n\n---\n\n## Step 5: Create Your First Template\n\nBefore you can send bulk messages, you need at least one approved template.\n\n1. Go to **Settings → Templates** in Waptrix\n2. Click **New Template**\n3. Choose category: **Marketing**, **Utility**, or **Authentication**\n4. Write your template body. Use {{1}}, {{2}} for variables\n5. Add a header image if needed\n6. Add buttons (Quick Reply or URL)\n7. Click **Submit to Meta**\n\nMeta reviews templates within 24 hours. You'll receive an email when approved.\n\n---\n\n## Step 6: Import Your Contacts\n\n1. Go to **Contacts** in Waptrix\n2. Click **Import CSV**\n3. Upload your contacts file with columns: name, phone, email (optional)\n4. Map the columns\n5. Create a **Segment** to group contacts (e.g., \"Mumbai Customers\", \"VIP buyers\")\n\nMake sure every contact has explicitly opted in to receive WhatsApp messages from you.\n\n---\n\n## Step 7: Launch Your First Campaign\n\n1. Go to **Campaigns → Create Campaign**\n2. Select your approved template\n3. Select your contact segment\n4. Set send time (now or scheduled)\n5. Click **Launch**\n\nWaptrix handles the sending, tracks delivery, and updates you with real-time stats.\n\n---\n\n## Common Setup Mistakes to Avoid\n\n**Mistake 1: Using a number already on WhatsApp**\nYou'll get an error during verification. Delete your existing WhatsApp account on that number first (Settings → Account → Delete My Account).\n\n**Mistake 2: Business name mismatch**\nYour WABA display name must match your business name. Meta rejects names that look like spam.\n\n**Mistake 3: Skipping Business Verification**\nWithout Business Verification, you're stuck at Tier 1 (1,000 messages/day). Complete verification to unlock higher limits.\n\n**Mistake 4: Using prohibited template language**\nMarketing templates can't contain certain phrases. Read Meta's template guidelines before writing.\n\n---\n\n## What Happens Next\n\nOnce you're set up, you can:\n- Send broadcast campaigns to thousands of contacts\n- Set up automated responses for common questions\n- Create multi-step drip sequences\n- Track delivery, read, and response rates\n- Manage all customer conversations in one inbox\n\n[Get started with Waptrix for free →](https://waptrix.in/pricing)",
